    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1729">

                <pb facs="1106" n="990" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg990"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 419.11D29/53.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Price to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Panama</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-04-28">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 28, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Vigorous action continued in the Cocoa Grove matter. Pursuant to your telegram of
                    April 20, Panaman Minister for Foreign Affairs on Saturday promised formal reply
                    to-day advising at least that judge in charge of case would render decision at
                    once and the same would be reviewed by Supreme Court promptly and their decree
                    given within 15 days. Reply not received to-day. Reference to testimony made by
                    Panaman Minister for Foreign Affairs foreshadows, I believe, a judicial
                    whitewashing. I shall make another demand in the morning.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Price</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
